    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1895-96/document/70> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493295806/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """[ HO’s designs]
came, he was evidently (from the tone of his letter) quite out of his senses with delight, and pressed upon them those very designs which  we  had taught him to see were his best, leaving nothing for us. Consequently, with the best will in the world, we cannot help him.
No doubt he will be angry and quarrel with Bernhard. I hope not, but it does seem hard for men to keep friends. They expect too much reasonableness from each other, and each is too intent upon his own “struggle for life”- 
However, in this instance I must say I think Obrist has acted very foolishly and thrown away a chance. It does not matter to us, for it is not in our line anyhow. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 70 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1895-96> .

